# Copy to server/.env (gitignored) and edit. Paths are relative to server/.
SCHOOL_COURSE_DIR=../../my-course
# Settings (settings.json) live here. If an old SQLite progress.db here still holds answers,
# explanations or views, the server refuses to start rather than leave them behind (RFC 3 §3.3).
SCHOOL_STATE_DIR=../../my-school-state
# Source material the course cites, mounted read-only at /sources and served at /papers/...
SCHOOL_SOURCES_DIR=../../my-course-sources
SCHOOL_MOUNTS=papers=/sources
# More courses for SCHOOL_COURSES and SCHOOL_UNTRUSTED_COURSES, mounted read-only at /library.
# Unset, /library is SCHOOL_COURSE_DIR again: the trusted course at /course under a second name.
# School compares folders by device and inode as well as by path, so it refuses to start when an
# untrusted course is, holds or sits inside a trusted one this way (flyingrobots/school#280). To
# serve untrusted courses, point this at a folder that does not hold SCHOOL_COURSE_DIR.
# School also walks the trusted folders, so part of one (a course's reference/, say) mounted where
# an untrusted course lives is refused too (flyingrobots/school#298). It cannot see a file or a
# subfolder of an untrusted course bind-mounted into a trusted course, a mount or the web folder:
# never mount either there.
# A trusted course, a mount or the web folder holding more than 10,000 folders is refused rather
# walked while SCHOOL_UNTRUSTED_COURSES is set: unset it, or point SCHOOL_MOUNTS or SCHOOL_WEB at a
# smaller folder.
# SCHOOL_LIBRARY_DIR=../../my-library
# The course store (RFC 7 §5.1): compose mounts the named volume `course-store` at /store and
# sets SCHOOL_COURSE_STORE=/store. Installed courses will live there; nothing installs yet. Set
# SCHOOL_COMPOSE_COURSE_STORE empty for no store, which keeps installing off. It is read only by
# compose, so a SCHOOL_COURSE_STORE exported on the host for running the server there never reaches
# the container. Any other value is a path inside the container, and the server refuses to start
# (exit 2) on one that is, holds or sits inside a course, the state folder, a mount, the web app or
# the framework, or that is a file.
# SCHOOL_COMPOSE_COURSE_STORE=

# No secret goes in this file (flyingrobots/school#123). The Postgres superuser's password,
# school_app's password and the bridge token live in the macOS Keychain, and `./school up` from the
# checkout reads them and starts compose (docs/topics/secrets/README.md). If an older .env still
# has SCHOOL_POSTGRES_PASSWORD, SCHOOL_APP_PASSWORD or SCHOOL_BRIDGE_TOKEN, `./school import` moves
# them into the Keychain and removes those lines; `./school up` refuses to start until it has.

# The `backup` service dumps the record every SCHOOL_BACKUP_INTERVAL_SECONDS and keeps the newest
# SCHOOL_BACKUP_KEEP dumps in the volume `backups` (docs/workflows/backup-and-restore/README.md).
# SCHOOL_BACKUP_INTERVAL_SECONDS=21600
# SCHOOL_BACKUP_KEEP=28


# Outside compose, two variables and two processes:
# - SCHOOL_MIGRATE_URL (for `bun migrate.ts` only): the owner's URL, a role that can create roles,
#   in practice the superuser. With SCHOOL_APP_PASSWORD it migrates and sets school_app's login.
# - SCHOOL_DATABASE_URL (for the server): postgres://school_app:<SCHOOL_APP_PASSWORD>@host:5432/db
#   (Bun.SQL). The server refuses the superuser, the owner, and a school_app with any of the extra
#   privileges its login check lists (docs/topics/architecture/README.md, "The login check"); never
#   grant school_app anything by hand. Or pglite:<dir> (PGlite on disk, no server, migrated by
#   the server itself; for development and tests only, since it does not fsync).
# There is no default: the server refuses to start without SCHOOL_DATABASE_URL. Any password may
# instead be given as a file, which wins over the plain variable: SCHOOL_APP_PASSWORD_FILE, and
# SCHOOL_MIGRATE_PASSWORD_FILE or SCHOOL_DATABASE_PASSWORD_FILE for a URL that names no password.
# compose.yaml does exactly that.

# The name School is reached by on your tailnet. Without it, every request through
# `tailscale serve` is refused; only localhost works.
SCHOOL_ALLOWED_HOSTS=school.example.ts.net

# Explanation grading. The bridge runs on the host (bun bridge/bridge.ts) and reads the same token
# from the Keychain as `./school up` gives the server; leave this unset to save explanations
# without grading them.
# SCHOOL_BRIDGE_URL=http://host.docker.internal:4748
